ience, technical (weather, computers). Weaknesses: communication tone, pretentiousness may affect crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate C: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, but unfriendly, eats unhealthily. Strengths: situational awareness, technical competence, leadership. Weaknesses: unfriendly (crew cooperation), unhealthy habits maybe affect reliability.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as loner. Strengths: problem solving, responsibility, concentration. Weaknesses: moodiness, loner (crew cooperation), maybe stress resilience unknown.\n\nWe need to start discussion. Choose a candidate? Perhaps Candidate B seems balanced: reliability, stress, technical, but communication issues. Candidate A has decision speed and attention but communication issues. Candidate C strong technical but unfriendly. Candidate D strong problem solving but moody.\n\nMaybe start with Candidate B as leading candidate, noting strengths and concerns, and propose as provisional recommendation, while noting need to discuss others.\n\nLet's produce public message: state vote for Candidate B, reference that we haven't discussed others yet, give evidence: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical), but pretentious and wrong tone (crew cooperation). Implication: B is strong but we need to compare with others.\n\nProceed."}
